The {{nihongo|'''Kurokawa Clan'''|黒川氏|Kurokawa-shi}} was a [[Sanese clan|Sanese samurai clan]] and later on the dynasty which established [[Kaneda]]. 

Initially ruled the [[Yura Province]] in southern court ([[Nakamizu]]), Kurokawa clan was able to establish trading post across [[Shendan Ocean]] over to [[Lurandia]] on 1478 in order to ensure the monopoly over inter-oceanic trading with Native Lurandian and Zong's Lurandia colony ([[Sinchew]]) with [[Ishiyama]] as the main entry gateway port to Sanese archipelago. However in 1587, [[Siege of Ishiyama (1587)|conflict with Shinozaki clan]] subsequently causes Kurokawa clan to lose its power and significance over their homeland and start focusing more on its settlement of [[Nanaimo]]. With the Kawaei-clan secured its prominence as the unifying force of Nakamizu, Kurokawa clan maintain cordial relationship with Kawaei, owning the port city of [[Kurokawa]] and Kurokawa Domain which named after the clan while continues to expand their settlement in Lurandia. Kurokawa clan also maintain decent relationship with [[Sea Wolves]] and other Umijin clans as their envoys on their trading and settlement activities over Shendan Ocean.

Kurokawa clan is a notable [[w:Watatsumi|Watatsumi]] worshiper established Watatsumi shrines all over Yura Province and Kaneda. 



